.TH ST 1 st-wl\-VERSION
.SH NAME
st-wl \- simple terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B st-wl
.RB [ \-av ]
.RB [ \-A
.IR alpha ]
.RB [ \-U
.IR alpha ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR class ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR font ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR iofile ]
.RB [ \-T
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR line ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR windowid ]
.RB [[ \-e ]
.IR command
.RI [ arguments ...]]
.PP
.B st-wl
.RB [ \-av ]
.RB [ \-A
.IR alpha ]
.RB [ \-U
.IR alpha ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR class ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR font ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR iofile ]
.RB [ \-T
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR windowid ]
.RB \-l
.IR line
.RI [ stty_args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B st-wl
is a simple terminal emulator for Wayland. It sets
.B TERM
to
.I @TERMNAME@
and opens a window of @COLS@ columns by @ROWS@ rows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
disable alternate screens in terminal
.TP
.BI \-A " alpha"
defines the background opacity, from 0.0 (transparent) to 1.0 (opaque)
(default @ALPHA@).
.TP
.BI \-U " alpha"
defines the background opacity used when the window does not have keyboard
focus, and for cells drawn in the unfocusedpanebg color (e.g. inactive tmux
panes) (default @ALPHA_UNFOCUSED@). See
.B FOCUS TRANSPARENCY
below.
.TP
.BI \-c " class"
defines the window class, used as the Wayland app_id (default '@TERMCLASS@').
.TP
.BI \-f " font"
defines the
.I font
to use when st-wl is run (default: the built-in JetBrains Mono Nerd Font at
size @FONTSIZE@).
.TP
.BI \-n " name"
is accepted for compatibility with st and ignored; Wayland has no instance
names.
.TP
.BI \-o " iofile"
writes all the I/O to
.I iofile.
This feature is useful when recording st-wl sessions. A value of "-" means
standard output.
.TP
.BI \-T " title"
defines the window title (default 'st-wl', or the command name when a command
is given).
.TP
.BI \-t " title"
same as
.BR \-T .
.TP
.BI \-w " windowid"
is accepted for compatibility with st and ignored; Wayland does not support
embedding windows.
.TP
.BI \-l " line"
use a tty
.I line
instead of a pseudo terminal.
.I line
should be a (pseudo-)serial device (e.g. /dev/ttyS0 on Linux for serial port
0).
When this flag is given
remaining arguments are used as flags for
.BR stty(1).
By default st-wl initializes the serial line to 8 bits, no parity, 1 stop bit
and a 38400 baud rate. The speed is set by appending it as last argument
(e.g. 'st-wl -l /dev/ttyS0 115200'). Arguments before the last one are
.BR stty(1)
flags. If you want to set odd parity on 115200 baud use for example 'st-wl -l
/dev/ttyS0 parenb parodd 115200'. Set the number of bits by using for
example 'st-wl -l /dev/ttyS0 cs7 115200'. See
.BR stty(1)
for more arguments and cases.
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.TP
.BI \-e " command " [ " arguments " "... ]"
st-wl executes
.I command
instead of the shell.  If this is used it
.B must be the last option
on the command line, as in xterm / rxvt.
This option is only intended for compatibility,
and all the remaining arguments are used as a command
even without it.
.SH SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Break
Send a break in the serial line.
Break key is obtained in PC keyboards
pressing at the same time control and pause.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Print Screen
Toggle if st-wl should print to the
.I iofile.
.TP
.B Shift-Print Screen
Print the full screen to the
.I iofile.
.TP
.B Print Screen
Print the selection to the
.I iofile.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-Page Up
Increase font size.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-Page Down
Decrease font size.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-Home
Reset to default font size.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-y
Paste from the clipboard selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-c
Copy the selected text to the clipboard selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-v
Paste from the clipboard selection.
.TP
.B Shift-Insert
Paste from the clipboard selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Insert
Copy the selected text to the clipboard selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-o
Increase the background opacity by 0.05.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-p
Decrease the background opacity by 0.05.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Alt-o
Increase the unfocused background opacity by 0.05.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Alt-p
Decrease the unfocused background opacity by 0.05.
.TP
.B F11
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-Return
Open a new st-wl in the current working directory.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-F1
Cycle through the kitty graphics debug display modes.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-F6
Dump the kitty graphics state to stderr.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-F7
Unload all kitty graphics images from memory.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-F8
Toggle showing kitty graphics images.
.SH FOCUS TRANSPARENCY
The background is drawn with the
.B \-A
opacity while the window has keyboard focus and fades to the
.B \-U
opacity when it loses focus.
.PP
st-wl cannot see tmux panes, so inactive panes are dimmed through a sentinel
background color. Every cell whose background is exactly the
.I \%unfocusedpanebg
color from config.h (default #@UNFOCUSEDPANEBG@) is drawn with the default background
color at the
.B \-U
opacity. Let tmux paint inactive panes with that color by adding this to
.IR ~/.tmux.conf :
.PP
.RS
.nf
set \-as terminal\-features 'st*:RGB'
set \-g window\-style        'bg=#@UNFOCUSEDPANEBG@'
set \-g window\-active\-style 'bg=terminal'
.fi
.RE
.PP
The RGB feature makes tmux send the color unchanged instead of mapping it to the
256 color palette. Only cells with the default background are dimmed;
programs that paint their own background are not. Set
.I \%unfocusedpanebg
to \-1 to disable this.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
.B st-wl
can be customized by creating a custom config.h and (re)compiling the source
code. This keeps it fast, secure and simple.
